        <h2 id="whats-stocked" class="scroll-mt-24 text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
          1. What Home Depot Actually Stocks
        </h2>

        <p>
          In-store, expect two names: <strong>Sakrete PermaSand</strong> and <strong>Quikrete PowerLoc</strong>, usually in the masonry or hardscape aisle near the pavers rather than with the bagged play sand. Colours are typically limited to tan and grey, which covers the majority of concrete pavers and satisfies nobody with unusual stone.
        </p>

        <p>
          Online is a different catalogue. <strong>Alliance Gator Maxx G2</strong> and <strong>DOMINATOR</strong> are commonly listed for delivery or store pickup even where no store within an hour has a bag on the shelf. That matters, because those are the products rated for wide joints and irregular flagstone — the exact cases where the in-store options are the wrong purchase. The catch is lead time: they need ordering days ahead, and the classic sequence of failure is discovering that on the morning the pavers are laid and buying whatever is in the aisle instead.
        </p>

        <p>
          Availability moves around by region and season, and the honest advice is to check your own store's stock online before driving over, particularly in spring when hardscape products sell through quickly. Store apps show live inventory by location, and it is worth checking two nearby stores rather than assuming the larger one has more.
        </p>

