        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your joints are standard width and you are going today, <strong class="text-white">Quikrete PowerLoc</strong> or <strong class="text-white">Sakrete PermaSand</strong> will do the job perfectly well — PowerLoc gives slightly better coverage per dollar in 50 lb bags. If your joints are wide, your stone is irregular, or you want the best odds against haze, order <strong class="text-white">Alliance Gator Maxx G2</strong> online a few days ahead.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Then buy one bag more than you think, measure your joints before you leave the house, and remember that the product is rarely what fails. A dry surface, joints filled to depth, faces blown clean, and watering exactly as the bag says will make the cheapest bag on the shelf outperform the most expensive one applied in a hurry.
          </p>
